    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1196">

                <pb facs="1437" n="1423" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/2–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-16">February 16,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received February 16—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. Venezuela’s official declaration<anchor n="44" xml:id="d1196-f1"/> of
                    recognition of the existence of state of belligerency between itself on the one
                    hand and Germany and Japan on the other, issued in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gazette Oficial</hi> last night, was published as Foreign Office communiqué
                    in all Caracas papers this morning. This declaration states that Ambassador
                    Escalante has full powers to sign document of Venezuela’s adherence to United
                    Nations Declaration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1196-f1" n="44" xml:id="d1196-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the declaration, see note from the Venezuelan Chargé, February 16,
                    1945, released to the press February 20, printed in Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, February 25, 1945, p. 292. For reply by
                    the Acting Secretary of State on February 19, remarks by the Venezuelan
                    Ambassador upon signing the United Nations Declaration on February 20, and
                    remarks by the Acting Secretary of State upon that occasion, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, pp. 293–294.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
